ation tests for the command, 2 pre-existing utility tests). Test coverage includes valid YAML patterns, invalid YAML patterns, edge cases, and CLI behavior. Integration tests use subprocess spawning for realistic end-to-end verification.\n\n**Code Style**: Consistent with the existing project style (minimal, clean TypeScript). No unnecessary comments or over-engineering. Helper functions are well-named and focused.\n\n**Conservative Bias**: The validator follows the design principle of accepting input when uncertain, which minimizes false positives -- an important quality for a developer-facing validation tool.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. All acceptance criteria are verified and the implementation is complete. No blocking issues exist.\n2. The README has been updated to document the new `validate` subcommand and the new source files, matching the documentation impact requirements in the design.\n3. Consider adding the `validate` command to the `package.json` scripts section as a convenience alias (e.g., `\"validate\": \"bun run src/index.ts validate\"`) in a future iteration, though this is not required by the current requirements.\n\n## Verification Evidence\n\n### Live CLI Tests\n\n```\n$ bun run src/index.ts Alice\nHello, Alice!\nEXIT: 0\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/test_valid.yaml\n/tmp/test_valid.yaml: valid YAML\nEXIT: 0\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate\nUsage: validate <file>\nEXIT: 1\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/nonexistent_xyz.yaml\nError: File not found: /tmp/nonexistent_xyz.yaml\nEXIT: 1\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/test_invalid.yaml\n/tmp/test_invalid.yaml:2: Tab character used for indentation (YAML forbids tabs for indentation)\nEXIT: 1\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/test_empty.yaml\n/tmp/test_empty.yaml: valid YAML\nEXIT: 0\n```\n\n### Test Suite Results\n\n```\nbun test v1.3.3\n\n 75 pass\n  0 fail\n 128 expect() calls\nRan 75 tests across 3 files. [117.00ms]\n```\n\n### Key Code References\n\n| File | Lines