        "content": "# Hypothesis Document: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Created**: 2026-03-01 | **Status**: VALIDATED\n\n## Hypotheses\n### HYP-001: From-Scratch TypeScript YAML Syntax Checker Feasibility\n**Risk Level**: HIGH\n**Status**: CONFIRMED\n**Statement**: A from-scratch TypeScript YAML syntax checker can correctly identify common syntax errors (unclosed quotes, tab indentation, unbalanced flow indicators, bad block scalar headers) while not producing false positives on valid YAML for common use cases (nested mappings, sequences, block scalars, flow collections, comments, document markers).\n**Context**: The design calls for a custom YAML syntax checker (no external libraries) as the core of the validate command. If the checker produces false positives on valid YAML or fails to detect common errors, the feature will not meet its requirements.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: The checker correctly validates a representative test suite of 15+ valid YAML patterns (simple k/v, nested maps, sequences, block scalars, flow collections, comments, quoted strings, document markers, empty files) AND correctly rejects 8+ invalid patterns (tab indentation, unclosed quotes, unbalanced braces/brackets, bad block scalar headers) with accurate line numbers.\n- REJECT if: The checker produces false positives on any of the common valid YAML patterns listed above, OR fails to detect tab indentation or unclosed quote errors, OR reports incorrect line numbers for detected errors.\n**Suggested Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n\n## Validation Findings\n\n### HYP-001 Findings\n**Validated**: 2026-03-01T01:27:00Z\n**Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n**Result**: CONFIRMED\n\n**Evidence**:\n\nA prototype from-scratch TypeScript YAML syntax checker (~230 lines) was implemented and tested against a comprehensive test suite of 56 test cases across three test runs. The checker uses a line-by-line scanner with state tracking for flow collection depth, block scalar mode, and quote context.\n\n**Test Run 1 -- Core Test Suite (34 tests, 34 passed)**:\n- 23 valid YAML patterns tested (all accepted correctly, zero false positives):\n  - V01: Empty file\n  - V02: Simple key-value pairs\n  - V03: Nested mappings (3 levels deep)\n  - V04: Sequences (lists)\n  - V05: Literal block scalar (|)\n  - V06: Folded block scalar (>)\n  - V07: Flow mapping ({})\n  - V08: Flow sequence ([])\n  - V09: Full-line and inline comments\n  - V10: Double-quoted strings with escapes\n  - V11: Single-quoted strings with escaped apostrophe\n  - V12: Document markers (--- and ...)\n  - V13: Mixed mappings + sequences (complex nested)\n  - V14: Boolean and null values\n  - V15: Whitespace-only file\n  - V16: Comment-only file\n  - V17: Block scalars with chomping indicators (|+ and >-)\n  - V18: Block scalar with explicit indentation indicator (|2)\n  - V19: Nested flow collections ([[1,2],[3,4]])\n  - V20: Multiline flow collection\n  - V21: Colons in values (URLs, quoted strings)\n  - V22: Document end marker only\n  - V23: Root-level sequence of mappings\n\n- 11 invalid YAML patterns tested (all rejected correctly with accurate line numbers):\n  - I01: Tab indentation (line 2) -- detected correctly\n  - I02: Unclosed double quote (line 1) -- detected correctly\n  - I03: Unclosed single quote (line 1) -- detected correctly\n  - I04: Unbalanced opening brace -- detected at EOF\n  - I05: Unbalanced opening bracket -- detected at EOF\n  - I06: Unexpected closing brace (line 1) -- detected correctly\n  - I07: Unexpected closing bracket (line 1) -- detected correctly\n  - I08: Invalid block scalar header \"|invalid\" (line 1) -- detected correctly\n  - I09: Tab on first line (line 1) -- detected correctly\n  - I10: Mixed space-tab indentation (line 2) -- detected correctly\n  - I11: Invalid folded block scalar header \">abc\" (line 1) -- detected correctly\n\n**Test Run 2 -- Edge Cases (18 tests, 18 passed)**:\n- 15 tricky valid patterns (all accepted, zero false positives):\n  - E01: Colon in unquoted URL value (http://example.com:8080/path)\n  - E02: Hash in quoted string (not a comment) (\"#ff0000\")\n  - E03: Curly braces in quoted string (\"{name} is {age} years old\")\n  - E04: Square brackets in quoted string ('[a-z]+')\n  - E05: Multiple YAML documents separated by ---\n  - E06: Anchors and aliases (&defaults, *defaults)\n  - E07: Complex nested mix of block and flow styles\n  - E08: Empty mapping value (key followed by newline)\n  - E09: Root sequence of flow mappings\n  - E10: Quoted mapping keys\n  - E11: Multiline flow mapping\n  - E12: Block scalar followed by de-indented content\n  - E13: Empty sequence items (bare dashes)\n  - E14: Unicode content\n  - E15: Very long line (10,000 characters)\n\n- 3 tricky invalid patterns (all rejected correctly):\n  - E16: Tab in middle of indentation (3 spaces + tab, line 2) -- detected correctly\n  - E17: Unclosed quote in sequence item value (line 2) -- detected correctly\n  - E18: Invalid block scalar header \"|abc\" (line 1) -- detected correctly\n\n**Test Run 3 -- Realistic Production Files (4 tests, 4 passed)**:\n- Kubernetes Deployment manifest (54 lines) -- accepted correctly\n- GitHub Actions CI config (39 lines) -- accepted correctly\n- Docker Compose config (45 lines) -- accepted correctly\n- Complex application config with block scalars, flow collections, nested structures (57 lines) -- accepted correctly\n\n**Architecture of the Prototype**:\nThe checker is structured as:\n1. A main `validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult` function (~80 lines)\n2. Helper: `stripInlineComment()` -- respects quoted strings when stripping comments\n3. Helper: `checkUnclosedQuotes()` -- detects unclosed single/double quotes in mapping values and sequence items\n4. Helper: `checkFlowIndicators()` -- tracks { } [ ] nesting depth across lines, respects quotes\n5. Helper: `isQuotedStringClosed()` -- handles escaped quotes in both quote styles\n6. State tracking: `flowDepthBraces`, `flowDepthBrackets`, `inBlockScalar`, `blockScalarIndent`\n\nTotal prototype: approximately 230 lines of TypeScript (pure function, no dependencies).\n\n**Sources**:\n- Prototype: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/yaml-validator.ts` (DISPOSABLE)\n- Test harness 1: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/test-harness.ts` (DISPOSABLE)\n- Test harness 2: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/edge-cases.ts` (DISPOSABLE)\n- Test harness 3: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/realistic-test.ts` (DISPOSABLE)\n- Executed with Bun 1.3.3 on the project's runtime\n\n**Implications for Design**:\nThe from-scratch TypeScript YAML syntax checker approach described in the design document is feasible and effective. Key findings for the feature designer:\n\n1. **Zero false positives achieved**: Across 42 distinct valid YAML patterns (including production-realistic files like Kubernetes manifests, CI configs, and Docker Compose files), the checker produced zero false positives. The conservative-bias design principle works well.\n\n2. **All required error types detected**: Tab indentation, unclosed quotes (single and double), unbalanced flow indicators (braces and brackets, both open and close), and invalid block scalar headers are all correctly detected with accurate line numbers.\n\n3. **Implementation complexity is manageable**: The prototype is approximately 230 lines of TypeScript with no external dependencies. The line-by-line scanning approach with minimal state tracking (flow depth, block scalar mode) is sufficient for the required checks.\n\n4. **Key design patterns validated**:\n   - Quote-aware processing is essential for comments, flow indicators, and quote checking itself\n   - Block scalar state tracking requires remembering the parent indentation level\n   - Flow indicator tracking must span multiple lines (multiline flow collections)\n   - Inline comment stripping must precede other checks but respect quoted strings\n\n5. **Known limitations (acceptable per design doc's conservative bias)**:\n   - Does not detect all possible YAML syntax errors (e.g., duplicate keys, invalid anchor references)\n   - Does not validate indentation consistency beyond tab detection\n   - These are explicitly out of scope per the requirements and design documents\n\n## Summary\n| Hypothesis | Risk | Result | Implication |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------|\n| HYP-001 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | From-scratch TypeScript YAML checker is feasible: 56/56 tests passed with zero false positives on valid YAML and correct detection+line numbers for all required error types |\n"
