        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 4 days\n**Started**: 2026-03-01\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a `validate` subcommand to the existing CLI entry point that accepts a file path, reads the file, runs a from-scratch YAML syntax checker, and reports whether the file is syntactically valid YAML. On success it prints confirmation to stdout (exit 0); on failure it prints file path, line number, and error description to stderr (exit 1). No new dependencies are introduced.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2] - Independent modules: T1 modifies routing logic, T2 implements pure validation functions. No shared interfaces beyond the import that T1 will use.\n2. [T3, T4] - T3 wires T1+T2 together; T4 tests T2. Both depend on T2 being complete but are independent of each other.\n3. [T5] - Integration tests require the full CLI flow (T1 + T3) to be functional.\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T3 -> T2 (interface: T3 calls `validateYaml()` from T2)\n- T3 -> T1 (interface: T1 must import and call `runValidateCommand()` from T3)\n- T4 -> T2 (interface: T4 imports and tests functions from T2)\n- T5 -> [T1, T3] (build: T5 tests the full CLI which requires both routing and command handler)\n\n**Critical Path**: T2 -> T3 -> T5\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Independent Modules\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Add subcommand routing to CLI entry point for \"validate\" command `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-entry-point-modification-srcindexts](design.md#33-entry-point-modification-srcindexts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `src/index.ts` imports `runValidateCommand` from `./validate-command` via static import\n    - [ ] When `process.argv[2] === \"validate\"`, execution delegates to `runValidateCommand(process.argv)` with `await`\n    - [ ] When `process.argv[2]` is not `\"validate\"`, existing greeting behavior is preserved unchanged (argument treated as name, defaults to \"World\")\n    - [ ] No dynamic imports are used; import is static for type safety\n    - [ ] Top-level `await` is used (supported in Bun ES modules)\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement from-scratch YAML syntax checker module `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-yaml-validator-module-srcyaml-validatorts](design.md#31-yaml-validator-module-srcyaml-validatorts)\n\n    **Effort**: 10 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New file `src/yaml-validator.ts` is created\n    - [ ] Exports `YamlValidationResult` type (discriminated union of `YamlValidationSuccess` and `YamlValidationError`)\n    - [ ] Exports `validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult` as a pure function (no side effects, no file I/O, no console output)\n    - [ ] Detects tab indentation and reports correct line number\n    - [ ] Detects unclosed quoted strings (single and double) and reports correct line number\n    - [ ] Detects invalid mapping syntax (colon without proper spacing) in applicable contexts\n    - [ ] Detects unbalanced flow indicators (`{`, `}`, `[`, `]`) and reports correct line number\n    - [ ] Detects duplicate document markers in invalid positions\n    - [ ] Detects invalid block scalar headers (bad characters after `|` or `>`)\n    - [ ] Detects indentation consistency errors (dedent to never-established level)\n    - [ ] Maintains state across lines: indentation stack, block scalar context, flow collection context\n    - [ ] Lines starting with `#` (after optional whitespace) are skipped as comments\n    - [ ] Inline comments (` #`) are stripped before checking\n    - [ ] Returns first error found (early exit)\n    - [ ] Line numbers are 1-indexed\n    - [ ] Conservative bias: accepts input as valid when uncertain\n    - [ ] Empty string input returns `{ valid: true }`\n\n### Command Wiring and Unit Tests\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement validate command handler with CLI orchestration `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-validate-command-module-srcvalidate-commandts](design.md#32-validate-command-module-srcvalidate-commandts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New file `src/validate-command.ts` is created\n    - [ ] Exports `async function runValidateCommand(args: string[]): Promise<void>`\n    - [ ] Extracts file path from `args[3]` (index 0=bun, 1=script, 2=\"validate\", 3=file path)\n    - [ ] When `args[3]` is undefined, prints `Usage: validate <file>` to stderr and calls `process.exit(1)`\n    - [ ] Reads file using `Bun.file(filePath).text()` wrapped in try/catch\n    - [ ] When file is not found, prints `Error: File not found: <filePath>` to stderr and exits 1\n    - [ ] When file is not readable, prints `Error: Cannot read file: <filePath>` to stderr and exits 1\n    - [ ] On valid YAML, prints `<filePath>: valid YAML` to stdout via `console.log` and exits 0\n    - [ ] On invalid YAML, prints `<filePath>:<line>: <message>` to stderr via `console.error` and exits 1\n    - [ ] Calls `validateYaml(content)` from `src/yaml-validator.ts` for validation logic\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Write comprehensive unit tests for YAML syntax checker `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#t4-yaml-validator-unit-tests-srcyaml-validatortestts](design.md#t4-yaml-validator-unit-tests-srcyaml-validatortestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New file `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` is created using `bun:test` framework\n    - [ ] Tests for valid YAML: empty string, simple key-value, nested mappings, lists/sequences, comments, multi-line strings (block scalars), document markers (`---`, `...`), mixed content, quoted strings, flow collections, boolean/null/numeric values\n    - [ ] Tests for invalid YAML: tab indentation, unclosed double quote, unclosed single quote, unbalanced braces, unbalanced brackets, invalid block scalar header, bad indentation, mapping without proper colon spacing\n    - [ ] Each invalid YAML test verifies `valid === false`, correct `line` number, and non-empty `message` string\n    - [ ] Edge case tests: file with only comments, file with only whitespace, file with document end marker only, very long lines, unicode content\n    - [ ] All tests trace to FR-003 (syntax validation) and FR-005 (error details) requirements\n\n### Integration Tests\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Write integration tests for validate command CLI behavior `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#t5-command-integration-tests-srcvalidate-commandtestts](design.md#t5-command-integration-tests-srcvalidate-commandtestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New file `src/validate-command.test.ts` is created using `bun:test` framework\n    - [ ] Tests use `Bun.spawn()` or direct function calls with stdout/stderr capture\n    - [ ] Test: missing file argument produces usage message on stderr and exit code 1\n    - [ ] Test: non-existent file produces error message on stderr and exit code 1\n    - [ ] Test: valid YAML file produces success message on stdout and exit code 0\n    - [ ] Test: invalid YAML file produces error with line number on stderr and exit code 1\n    - [ ] Test: empty file produces success result (valid YAML) and exit code 0\n    - [ ] Test: existing greeting behavior preserved when first argument is not \"validate\"\n    - [ ] All tests trace to FR-001, FR-002, FR-004, FR-005, BR-004 requirements\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Scripts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] README.md Scripts section documents the `validate` subcommand: `bun run dev validate <file>` -- Validate a YAML file for syntax errors\n    - [ ] Section reflects the correct invocation pattern and describes the command purpose\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update README.md - Structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] README.md Structure section lists `src/yaml-validator.ts` and `src/validate-command.ts` as new project files\n    - [ ] Section reflects the updated project directory layout\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n- [ ] AC-001a: Running `bun run dev validate <file>` invokes the YAML validation logic\n- [ ] AC-001b: Running `bun run dev` without `validate` preserves the existing greeting behavior\n- [ ] AC-002a: When a valid file path is provided, the system reads and validates that file\n- [ ] AC-002b: When no file path is provided, the system displays a usage message indicating that a file path is required\n- [ ] AC-002c: When the specified file does not exist or is not readable, the system displays a clear error message\n- [ ] AC-003a: A syntactically valid YAML file produces a \"valid\" result\n- [ ] AC-003b: A syntactically invalid YAML file produces an \"invalid\" result\n- [ ] AC-003c: An empty file is treated as valid YAML\n- [ ] AC-004a: The output message includes the file path and an indication that the file is valid\n- [ ] AC-004b: The process exits with code 0 on success\n- [ ] AC-005a: The error output includes the file path\n- [ ] AC-005b: The error output includes the line number of the syntax error\n- [ ] AC-005c: The error output includes a human-readable description of what is wrong\n- [ ] AC-005d: The process exits with a non-zero exit code on failure\n- [ ] AC-006a: The `package.json` file has no new entries in `dependencies` or `devDependencies`\n- [ ] AC-006b: No new `node_modules` packages are required at runtime\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All AC verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Docs updated\n"
