        "content": "# Feature Verification Report #1\n\n**Generated**: 2026-03-01T02:06:00Z\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Verification Scope**: all\n**KB Context**: -- Not loaded (no `.rp1/context/` directory found; consider running `/knowledge-build`)\n**Field Notes**: -- Not available\n\n## Executive Summary\n- Overall Status: VERIFIED\n- Acceptance Criteria: 16/16 verified (100%)\n- Implementation Quality: HIGH\n- Ready for Merge: YES\n\n## Field Notes Context\n**Field Notes Available**: -- No\n\n### Documented Deviations\nNone (no field-notes.md file present in feature directory)\n\n### Undocumented Deviations\nNone found. Implementation closely follows the design specification. Two design notes from `tasks.md` describe intentional conservative choices within the design philosophy:\n1. Mapping syntax check (colon without spacing) uses conservative bias and does not flag `key:value` patterns since they are valid unquoted scalars. This aligns with the design principle D6 (conservative bias).\n2. Document marker check accepts all `---`/`...` positions without flagging duplicates, as multiple document markers are valid in multi-document YAML. This is correct YAML behavior, not a deviation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Verification\n\n### FR-001: Subcommand Recognition\n\n**AC-001a**: Running `bun run dev validate <file>` invokes the YAML validation logic.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/index.ts`:10-11 - conditional branch `if (command === \"validate\")`\n- Evidence: Line 10 checks `process.argv[2] === \"validate\"` and line 11 calls `await runValidateCommand(process.argv)`. Live test confirmed: `bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/test_valid.yaml` outputs `/tmp/test_valid.yaml: valid YAML` with exit code 0.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-001b**: Running `bun run dev` without `validate` preserves the existing greeting behavior.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/index.ts`:12-14 - else branch for non-validate arguments\n- Evidence: Lines 12-14 fall through to the existing greeting logic: `const name = command ?? \"World\"; console.log(greet(name));`. Live test confirmed: `bun run src/index.ts Alice` outputs `Hello, Alice!` with exit code 0. Integration test in `src/validate-command.test.ts`:80-84 also verifies this.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-002: File Path Argument\n\n**AC-002a**: When a valid file path is provided, the system reads and validates that file.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:12-17 - file reading with `Bun.file(filePath)`\n- Evidence: Lines 12-17 use `Bun.file(filePath).exists()` for existence check, then `file.text()` to read content. Line 24 passes content to `validateYaml(content)`. Live test confirmed valid file is read and validated successfully.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-002b**: When no file path is provided, the system displays a usage message indicating that a file path is required.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:5-8 - missing argument check\n- Evidence: Lines 5-8: `if (!filePath) { console.error(\"Usage: validate <file>\"); process.exit(1); }`. Live test confirmed: running `validate` with no file argument outputs `Usage: validate <file>` to stderr with exit code 1. Integration test at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:33-38 verifies this.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-002c**: When the specified file does not exist or is not readable, the system displays a clear error message stating the file cannot be found or read.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:13-21 - file existence check and try/catch for read errors\n- Evidence: Line 13: `if (!(await file.exists()))` prints `Error: File not found: <filePath>` to stderr and exits 1. Lines 18-21: catch block prints `Error: Cannot read file: <filePath>` for permission/read errors. Live test confirmed: non-existent file produces `Error: File not found: /tmp/nonexistent_xyz.yaml` on stderr with exit code 1. Integration test at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:40-47 verifies this.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-003: Syntax Validation\n\n**AC-003a**: A syntactically valid YAML file produces a \"valid\" result.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator.ts`:226-350 - `validateYaml()` function returns `{ valid: true }` at line 350\n- Evidence: The function performs line-by-line scanning and returns `{ valid: true }` when no errors are detected. Live test confirmed: valid YAML content produces success output. 33 unit tests in `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` cover various valid YAML patterns (key-value, nested, lists, comments, block scalars, flow collections, quoted strings, etc.).\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003b**: A syntactically invalid YAML file produces an \"invalid\" result.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator.ts`:244-249 (tabs), 286-288 (block scalar), 300-301 (flow), 307-309 (quotes), 322-330 (indentation), 335-348 (unclosed flow)\n- Evidence: Multiple error detection paths return `{ valid: false, line: number, message: string }`. Live test confirmed: tab-indented YAML produces error output. 16 unit tests in `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` cover invalid YAML patterns (tabs, unclosed quotes, unbalanced braces/brackets, invalid block scalar headers, bad indentation).\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003c**: An empty file is treated as valid YAML (an empty document is valid YAML per the specification).\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator.ts`:227-229 - early return for empty/whitespace-only content\n- Evidence: Lines 227-229: `if (content.length === 0 || content.trim().length === 0) { return { valid: true }; }`. Live test confirmed: empty file produces `valid YAML` output with exit code 0. Unit test at `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`:7-10 and integration test at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:70-78 verify this.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-004: Success Output\n\n**AC-004a**: The output message includes the file path and an indication that the file is valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:27 - `console.log(\\`${filePath}: valid YAML\\`)`\n- Evidence: The success message format is exactly `<filePath>: valid YAML`, printed to stdout. Live test confirmed: `/tmp/test_valid.yaml: valid YAML` was printed to stdout. Integration test at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:55-56 asserts both `filePath` and `valid YAML` appear in stdout.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-004b**: The process exits with code 0.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:28 - `process.exit(0)`\n- Evidence: Line 28 explicitly calls `process.exit(0)` on valid YAML. Live test confirmed exit code 0. Integration test at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:54 asserts `exitCode` is 0.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-005: Failure Output with Error Details\n\n**AC-005a**: The error output includes the file path.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:30 - `console.error(\\`${filePath}:${result.line}: ${result.message}\\`)`\n- Evidence: The error format includes `filePath` as the first component. Live test confirmed: `/tmp/test_invalid.yaml:2: Tab character used for indentation...` includes the file path. Integration test at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:65 asserts `filePath` appears in stderr.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-005b**: The error output includes the line number of the syntax error.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:30 - `${result.line}` in error format; `src/yaml-validator.ts` uses 1-indexed `lineNum = i + 1` at line 240\n- Evidence: The error format is `<filePath>:<line>: <message>` (compiler-style). Live test confirmed line number 2 was reported for a tab error on line 2. Integration test at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:66 asserts `:\\d+:` pattern in stderr. Unit test at `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`:631-642 verifies 1-indexed line numbers.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-005c**: The error output includes a human-readable description of what is wrong.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:30 - `${result.message}` in error format; `src/yaml-validator.ts` provides descriptive messages\n- Evidence: Error messages are human-readable, e.g.: \"Tab character used for indentation (YAML forbids tabs for indentation)\", \"Unclosed quoted string\", \"Unexpected closing brace '}'\", \"Invalid block scalar header: invalid modifier 'invalid' after '|'\", \"Invalid indentation: dedent to a level that was not previously established\". Live test confirmed descriptive message output.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-005d**: The process exits with a non-zero exit code.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/validate-command.ts`:31 - `process.exit(1)` on invalid YAML; also lines 7, 15, 20 for other error cases\n- Evidence: All error paths call `process.exit(1)`. Live test confirmed exit code 1 for invalid YAML, missing argument, and non-existent file. Integration tests at `src/validate-command.test.ts`:35,43,64 all assert `exitCode` is 1.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-006: No New Dependencies\n\n**AC-006a**: The `package.json` file has no new entries in `dependencies` or `devDependencies` after the feature is implemented.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `package.json` - unchanged dependency sections\n- Evidence: `package.json` contains only `\"devDependencies\": { \"@types/bun\": \"latest\" }` and no `dependencies` section at all. No YAML libraries or any other new packages were added. The YAML validator is a from-scratch TypeScript implementation in `src/yaml-validator.ts`.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-006b**: No new `node_modules` packages are required at runtime for the feature to function.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator.ts` - pure TypeScript with no imports; `src/validate-command.ts` - imports only from local project files\n- Evidence: `yaml-validator.ts` has zero import statements -- it is a self-contained pure TypeScript module. `validate-command.ts` imports only `validateYaml` from `./yaml-validator` (local file). No external packages are required at runtime.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n## Implementation Gap Analysis\n\n### Missing Implementations\nNone. All 16 acceptance criteria are fully implemented and verified.\n\n### Partial Implementations\nNone. No acceptance criteria are partially implemented.\n\n### Implementation Issues\nNone. No incorrectly implemented criteria were found.\n\n## Code Quality Assessment\n\n**Architecture**: The implementation follows a clean three-module architecture as specified in the design:\n- `src/index.ts` (15 lines) -- minimal subcommand routing with static imports\n- `src/validate-command.ts` (33 lines) -- focused CLI orchestration with proper error handling\n- `src/yaml-validator.ts` (351 lines) -- self-contained YAML syntax checker with well-separated helper functions\n\n**Separation of Concerns**: Excellent. The YAML validator is a pure function with no side effects, no file I/O, and no console output. The command handler manages all I/O concerns. The entry point handles only routing.\n\n**Error Handling**: Comprehensive. All error paths are handled:\n- Missing argument: usage message to stderr, exit 1\n- File not found: explicit existence check before read, clear error message\n- Unreadable file: try/catch wrapping file read operations\n- Invalid YAML: structured error with file path, line number, and description\n\n**Type Safety**: The `YamlValidationResult` discriminated union type (`YamlValidationSuccess | YamlValidationError`) provides compile-time type narrowing. The function signature `validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult` is clear and well-typed.\n\n**Testing**: 75 tests across 3 files (67 unit tests for the validator, 6 integration tests for the command, 2 pre-existing utility tests). Test coverage includes valid YAML patterns, invalid YAML patterns, edge cases, and CLI behavior. Integration tests use subprocess spawning for realistic end-to-end verification.\n\n**Code Style**: Consistent with the existing project style (minimal, clean TypeScript). No unnecessary comments or over-engineering. Helper functions are well-named and focused.\n\n**Conservative Bias**: The validator follows the design principle of accepting input when uncertain, which minimizes false positives -- an important quality for a developer-facing validation tool.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. All acceptance criteria are verified and the implementation is complete. No blocking issues exist.\n2. The README has been updated to document the new `validate` subcommand and the new source files, matching the documentation impact requirements in the design.\n3. Consider adding the `validate` command to the `package.json` scripts section as a convenience alias (e.g., `\"validate\": \"bun run src/index.ts validate\"`) in a future iteration, though this is not required by the current requirements.\n\n## Verification Evidence\n\n### Live CLI Tests\n\n```\n$ bun run src/index.ts Alice\nHello, Alice!\nEXIT: 0\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/test_valid.yaml\n/tmp/test_valid.yaml: valid YAML\nEXIT: 0\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate\nUsage: validate <file>\nEXIT: 1\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/nonexistent_xyz.yaml\nError: File not found: /tmp/nonexistent_xyz.yaml\nEXIT: 1\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/test_invalid.yaml\n/tmp/test_invalid.yaml:2: Tab character used for indentation (YAML forbids tabs for indentation)\nEXIT: 1\n\n$ bun run src/index.ts validate /tmp/test_empty.yaml\n/tmp/test_empty.yaml: valid YAML\nEXIT: 0\n```\n\n### Test Suite Results\n\n```\nbun test v1.3.3\n\n 75 pass\n  0 fail\n 128 expect() calls\nRan 75 tests across 3 files. [117.00ms]\n```\n\n### Key Code References\n\n| File | Lines | Purpose |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| `src/index.ts` | 1-15 | Subcommand routing (AC-001a, AC-001b) |\n| `src/validate-command.ts` | 1-33 | CLI orchestration (AC-002a/b/c, AC-004a/b, AC-005a/b/c/d) |\n| `src/yaml-validator.ts` | 1-351 | YAML syntax checker (AC-003a/b/c) |\n| `src/yaml-validator.ts` | 226-229 | Empty content handling (AC-003c) |\n| `src/yaml-validator.ts` | 244-249 | Tab detection (AC-003b, AC-005b) |\n| `src/yaml-validator.ts` | 306-309 | Quote checking (AC-003b) |\n| `src/yaml-validator.ts` | 313-331 | Indentation validation (AC-003b) |\n| `src/yaml-validator.ts` | 335-348 | Unclosed flow detection (AC-003b) |\n| `package.json` | 1-15 | No new dependencies (AC-006a, AC-006b) |\n| `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` | 1-644 | 67 unit tests for validator |\n| `src/validate-command.test.ts` | 1-85 | 6 integration tests for CLI |\n"
