        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator-command/tasks.md",
        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 6 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 1.5 days\n**Started**: 2026-03-01\n\n## Overview\n\nA CLI command (`bun run validate-yaml <file>`) that validates a single YAML file for syntactic correctness using Bun's built-in `Bun.YAML.parse()` parser. Implemented as two modules -- a pure validation logic module and a CLI entry point -- following the existing project patterns. Zero new dependencies.\n\n**Known Limitation (HYP-002 REJECTED)**: Bun's YAML parser does NOT provide line/column position information in parse errors. The error message is always the generic `\"YAML Parse error: Unexpected token\"`. All error reporting is message-only without source positions. The `YamlValidationResult.error` type retains optional `line?`/`column?` fields for forward-compatibility, but they will not be populated. FR-002 AC-2 (\"include line number or position information when the underlying parser provides it\") is satisfied by omission since the parser does not provide it.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation module with no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend only on T1; CLI entry point and tests are independent of each other\n3. [T4] - Wiring depends on CLI entry point existing\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: T2 imports `validateYaml` and `YamlValidationResult` from T1)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: T3 imports `validateYaml` from T1 to test it)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: package.json script references `src/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create YAML validation logic module with types and pure validation function `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-validation-logic-module](design.md#31-validation-logic-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.ts` exists and exports `YamlValidationResult` interface with `valid: boolean` and optional `error?: { message: string; line?: number; column?: number }` fields\n    - [ ] File exports `validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult` function\n    - [ ] `validateYaml` calls `Bun.YAML.parse(content)` inside a try/catch block\n    - [ ] Valid YAML input returns `{ valid: true }` with no error field\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML input returns `{ valid: false, error: { message: \"...\" } }` where message is extracted from the caught SyntaxError\n    - [ ] The `error.line` and `error.column` fields are NOT populated (they remain `undefined`) because Bun's parser does not provide YAML-source position info (HYP-002 rejected); the implementation must not set these to JavaScript call-site line/column values\n    - [ ] Empty string input returns `{ valid: true }` (empty string is valid YAML)\n    - [ ] The function is pure -- no side effects, no file I/O, no console output\n    - [ ] Module uses ESM exports consistent with the project's `\"type\": \"module\"` configuration\n\n### CLI and Tests\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Create CLI entry point with argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting, and exit code management `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-cli-entry-point](design.md#32-cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 3 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.ts` exists and imports `validateYaml` from `./yaml-validator`\n    - [ ] Missing argument (no `process.argv[2]`): prints usage message to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] Usage message includes command syntax, argument description, and exit code documentation\n    - [ ] File not found (`Bun.file(path).exists()` returns false): prints `\"Error: File not found: <filepath>\"` to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] File reading uses `Bun.file(path).text()` to read contents as string\n    - [ ] Valid YAML file: prints `\"Valid YAML: <filepath>\"` to stdout and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML file: prints `\"Invalid YAML: <filepath>\"` followed by error message to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Error output shows the error message from `YamlValidationResult.error.message` only (no line/column position info is available per HYP-002 rejection); the actual output will be the generic Bun parser message (e.g., `\"YAML Parse error: Unexpected token\"`)\n    - [ ] Exit codes follow the scheme: 0=valid, 1=syntax error, 2=usage error\n    - [ ] Success output goes to stdout; all error/usage output goes to stderr\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Create unit tests for YAML validation logic covering valid, invalid, and edge case inputs `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` exists and imports `validateYaml` from `./yaml-validator`\n    - [ ] Test: valid simple YAML (`\"key: value\"`) returns `{ valid: true }` with no error property\n    - [ ] Test: valid multi-line YAML returns `{ valid: true }`\n    - [ ] Test: invalid YAML (`\"key: [invalid\"`) returns `{ valid: false }` with `error.message` as a non-empty string\n    - [ ] Test: invalid YAML result does NOT contain meaningful `error.line` or `error.column` values (assert they are `undefined`); this explicitly verifies the HYP-002 rejection -- Bun does not provide YAML-source position info\n    - [ ] Test: empty string returns `{ valid: true }` (empty is valid YAML per the YAML spec)\n    - [ ] Tests use `describe`/`test`/`expect` from `bun:test` consistent with the existing `src/utils.test.ts` pattern\n    - [ ] All tests pass when run via `bun test`\n\n### Script Wiring\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Add `validate-yaml` script entry to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-packagejson-script](design.md#33-packagejson-script)\n\n    **Effort**: 0.5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` `scripts` object contains `\"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"`\n    - [ ] No new entries added to `dependencies` or `devDependencies` (FR-005)\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate-yaml` invokes the CLI entry point\n    - [ ] Existing scripts (`dev`, `test`, `lint`, `format`) are unchanged\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Scripts section `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `README.md`\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] README.md Scripts section includes `bun run validate-yaml` with a description of its purpose (validate a YAML file for syntactic correctness)\n    - [ ] Existing script entries are preserved unchanged\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update README.md - Structure section `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `README.md`\n\n    **Section**: Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] README.md Structure section lists `src/validate-yaml.ts` (CLI entry point) and `src/yaml-validator.ts` (validation logic) with brief descriptions\n    - [ ] Existing file entries are preserved unchanged\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom `requirements.md`:\n\n- [ ] FR-001 AC-1: Given a path to a syntactically valid YAML file, the command outputs a success message and exits with code 0\n- [ ] FR-001 AC-2: Given a path to a syntactically invalid YAML file, the command outputs a failure message with error details and exits with a non-zero exit code\n- [ ] FR-002 AC-1: The error output includes a human-readable description of the syntax problem\n- [ ] FR-002 AC-2: The error output includes line number or position information when the underlying parser provides it (NOTE: Bun's parser does NOT provide this per HYP-002 rejection -- criterion satisfied by omission)\n- [ ] FR-003 AC-1: Given a non-existent file path, the command outputs a \"file not found\" error message\n- [ ] FR-003 AC-2: The exit code is non-zero for file not found\n- [ ] FR-004 AC-1: Invoking the command with no arguments outputs a usage/help message\n- [ ] FR-004 AC-2: The exit code is non-zero for missing argument\n- [ ] FR-005 AC-1: The package.json file has no new dependency entries after implementation\n- [ ] FR-005 AC-2: No new lock file entries are introduced for new packages\n- [ ] FR-006 AC-1: Exit code 0 is returned on successful validation\n- [ ] FR-006 AC-2: A non-zero exit code is returned on validation failure\n- [ ] FR-006 AC-3: A non-zero exit code is returned on usage errors\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks (T1-T4, TD1-TD2) completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] All tests pass (`bun test`)\n- [ ] Docs updated (README.md)\n- [ ] No new dependencies added to package.json\n"
