        "content": "# Feature Verification Report #001\n\n**Generated**: 2026-03-01T01:49:00Z\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Verification Scope**: all\n**KB Context**: -- Not loaded (no `.rp1/context/` directory found; consider running `/knowledge-build`)\n**Field Notes**: -- Not available (no `field-notes.md` found in feature directory)\n\n## Executive Summary\n- Overall Status: VERIFIED\n- Acceptance Criteria: 13/13 verified (100%)\n- Implementation Quality: HIGH\n- Ready for Merge: YES\n\nAll 13 acceptance criteria from requirements.md (FR-001 through FR-006) are fully implemented and verified through direct code examination and live CLI execution. The implementation follows the design specification precisely, introduces zero new dependencies, and all 7 unit tests pass. The code is clean, well-structured, and follows existing project conventions.\n\n## Field Notes Context\n**Field Notes Available**: -- No\n\n### Documented Deviations\nNone -- no field-notes.md file was found in the feature directory.\n\n### Undocumented Deviations\nNone found. The implementation matches the design specification in all verified areas. One known parser limitation (Bun YAML parser does not provide line/column position information) was documented in tasks.md under HYP-002 and addressed in the implementation by leaving those fields undefined. This is not an undocumented deviation; it was acknowledged during the build phase.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Verification\n\n### FR-001: Single File Validation\n\n**AC-1**: Given a path to a syntactically valid YAML file, the command outputs a success message and exits with code 0.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:31-33 -- `if (result.valid)` branch\n- Evidence: Lines 31-33 check `result.valid`, print `\"Valid YAML: <filepath>\"` to stdout via `console.log`, and call `process.exit(0)`. Live CLI test confirmed: running with a valid YAML file produced `Valid YAML: /tmp/test_valid.yaml` on stdout and exit code 0.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-2**: Given a path to a syntactically invalid YAML file, the command outputs a failure message with error details and exits with a non-zero exit code.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:34-38 -- `else` branch\n- Evidence: Lines 34-38 print `\"Invalid YAML: <filepath>\"` and `\"  Error: <message>\"` to stderr via `console.error`, then call `process.exit(1)`. Live CLI test confirmed: running with invalid YAML produced `Invalid YAML: /tmp/test_invalid.yaml` followed by `  Error: YAML Parse error: Unexpected token` on stderr and exit code 1.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-002: Actionable Error Reporting\n\n**AC-1**: The error output includes a human-readable description of the syntax problem.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml-validator.ts`:19-22 -- error message extraction in `validateYaml()`; `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:36 -- error output formatting\n- Evidence: The `validateYaml` function catches the parse error and extracts `e.message` (line 21). The CLI entry point displays this message via `console.error(\\`  Error: ${result.error?.message}\\`)` (line 36). Live test confirmed the output includes `\"YAML Parse error: Unexpected token\"` which is a human-readable description of the syntax problem.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-2**: The error output includes line number or position information when the underlying parser provides it.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml-validator.ts`:2-8 -- `YamlValidationResult` interface with optional `line?` and `column?` fields\n- Evidence: The `YamlValidationResult` type defines optional `line?: number` and `column?: number` fields (lines 6-7). The implementation correctly does NOT populate these fields because Bun's YAML parser does not provide position information in its error objects (documented in tasks.md as HYP-002 REJECTED). The criterion states \"when the underlying parser provides it\" -- since the parser does not provide it, the criterion is satisfied by the forward-compatible type definition and the absence of fabricated position data. Unit test `\"invalid YAML error has undefined line and column\"` explicitly verifies this behavior.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None. The parser limitation is a known constraint, not an implementation gap.\n\n### FR-003: File Not Found Handling\n\n**AC-1**: Given a non-existent file path, the command outputs a \"file not found\" (or equivalent) error message.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:20-26 -- file existence check and error message\n- Evidence: Line 21 calls `await file.exists()` using the `Bun.file()` API. Lines 23-26 check `if (!exists)` and print `\"Error: File not found: <filepath>\"` to stderr via `console.error`. Live CLI test confirmed: running with a nonexistent path produced `Error: File not found: /tmp/nonexistent_file.yaml` on stderr.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-2**: The exit code is non-zero.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:25 -- `process.exit(2)`\n- Evidence: Line 25 calls `process.exit(2)` in the file-not-found branch. Live CLI test confirmed exit code 2 for a nonexistent file path.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-004: Missing Argument Handling\n\n**AC-1**: Invoking the command with no arguments outputs a usage/help message.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:5-18 -- missing argument check and usage message\n- Evidence: Line 3 extracts `process.argv[2]` as `filePath`. Lines 5-18 check `if (!filePath)` and print a comprehensive usage message to stderr that includes: command syntax (`bun run validate-yaml <file>`), purpose description, argument documentation, and exit code reference. Live CLI test confirmed the full usage message is displayed when invoked with no arguments.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-2**: The exit code is non-zero.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:17 -- `process.exit(2)`\n- Evidence: Line 17 calls `process.exit(2)` in the missing-argument branch. Live CLI test confirmed exit code 2 when invoked with no arguments.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-005: Zero New Dependencies\n\n**AC-1**: The package.json file has no new dependency entries after implementation compared to before.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/package.json` -- dependencies section\n- Evidence: Compared the worktree `package.json` with the original at `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/package.json`. Both have identical dependency sections: `\"devDependencies\": { \"@types/bun\": \"latest\" }` with no `\"dependencies\"` field. The only difference is the addition of the `\"validate-yaml\"` script entry. Zero new packages were introduced.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-2**: No new package-lock, bun.lockb, or equivalent lock file entries are introduced for new packages.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: Filesystem check\n- Evidence: No `bun.lockb` or `package-lock.json` files exist in the worktree. The `.gitignore` includes `bun.lockb` as an ignored pattern. No lock file changes were introduced.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-006: Exit Code Conventions\n\n**AC-1**: Exit code 0 is returned on successful validation.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:33 -- `process.exit(0)`\n- Evidence: Line 33 calls `process.exit(0)` when `result.valid` is true. Live CLI test confirmed exit code 0 for valid YAML input.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-2**: A non-zero exit code is returned on validation failure.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:37 -- `process.exit(1)`\n- Evidence: Line 37 calls `process.exit(1)` when the YAML is syntactically invalid. Live CLI test confirmed exit code 1 for invalid YAML input. The use of exit code 1 specifically for validation failure (as opposed to exit code 2 for usage errors) follows the design specification.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-3**: A non-zero exit code is returned on usage errors.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/104c63d5/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:17,25 -- `process.exit(2)` in both usage error branches\n- Evidence: Line 17 calls `process.exit(2)` for missing arguments. Line 25 calls `process.exit(2)` for file-not-found. Live CLI tests confirmed exit code 2 for both scenarios. The use of exit code 2 for usage errors distinguishes them from validation failures (exit code 1), consistent with the design specification and standard CLI conventions.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n## Implementation Gap Analysis\n\n### Missing Implementations\nNone. All 13 acceptance criteria are fully implemented.\n\n### Partial Implementations\nNone. No acceptance criterion is only partially addressed.\n\n### Implementation Issues\nNone. No incorrectly implemented criteria were found.\n\n## Code Quality Assessment\n\n**Overall Quality: HIGH**\n\nThe implementation demonstrates strong adherence to software engineering best practices:\n\n1. **Separation of concerns**: The validation logic (`yaml-validator.ts`) is cleanly separated from the CLI I/O concerns (`validate-yaml.ts`), following the existing project pattern of `utils.ts`/`index.ts`. The validation function is pure with no side effects, making it independently testable.\n\n2. **Type safety**: The `YamlValidationResult` interface provides a well-structured return type with explicit optional fields for error details. The `error` property uses proper optional chaining in the CLI entry point (`result.error?.message`).\n\n3. **Error handling**: The `validateYaml` function uses a proper try/catch with `unknown` type annotation on the caught error and an `instanceof Error` guard before accessing `.message`, with a fallback string for non-Error exceptions.\n\n4. **Output routing**: Success messages go to stdout (`console.log`), error and usage messages go to stderr (`console.error`), following standard Unix conventions.\n\n5. **Exit code discipline**: Three distinct exit codes (0, 1, 2) correctly categorize outcomes as specified by FR-006 and design decision D4.\n\n6. **Test coverage**: 5 unit tests cover valid YAML, multi-line YAML, invalid YAML with error message, line/column absence verification (HYP-002), and the empty-string edge case. All use `describe`/`test`/`expect` from `bun:test`, matching the existing test patterns.\n\n7. **Project convention adherence**: File naming (kebab-case), module system (ESM), API choices (`Bun.file()`, `Bun.YAML.parse()`, `process.argv`), and code style all match the existing project conventions.\n\n8. **Documentation**: README.md is updated with both the new script in the Scripts section and the new files in the Structure section.\n\n**Minor observations** (not issues, just notes):\n- The CLI entry point uses top-level `await` (line 21: `await file.exists()`, line 28: `await file.text()`) which is supported in ESM modules with Bun. This is appropriate for the module type.\n- The usage message is comprehensive and includes argument description and exit code documentation, exceeding the minimum requirement.\n\n## Recommendations\n\nNo corrective action is needed. All acceptance criteria are verified. The following are optional enhancements for future consideration:\n\n1. **Integration test formalization**: The CLI integration scenarios (valid file, invalid file, file not found, no arguments) were verified manually during this review. Adding these as automated subprocess-based tests in a dedicated test file would provide regression protection.\n\n2. **Line/column forward-compatibility**: When Bun's YAML parser adds position information to error objects in the future, the `validateYaml` function could be updated to extract and return `line`/`column` values. The type system already accommodates this via the optional fields. Consider adding a tracking issue for this enhancement.\n\n## Verification Evidence\n\n### Source File Summary\n\n| File | Path | Lines | Purpose |\n|------|------|-------|---------|\n| yaml-validator.ts | `src/yaml-validator.ts` | 27 | Pure validation logic module with `YamlValidationResult` type and `validateYaml()` function |\n| validate-yaml.ts | `src/validate-yaml.ts` | 38 | CLI entry point with argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting, exit codes |\n| yaml-validator.test.ts | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` | 40 | 5 unit tests covering valid, invalid, and edge case inputs |\n| package.json | `package.json` | 16 | Added `validate-yaml` script; no new dependencies |\n| README.md | `README.md` | 21 | Updated Scripts and Structure sections |\n\n### Test Results\n\nAll 7 tests pass (5 in yaml-validator.test.ts + 2 in utils.test.ts):\n\n```\nbun test v1.3.3\n 7 pass\n 0 fail\n 16 expect() calls\nRan 7 tests across 2 files. [8.00ms]\n```\n\n### CLI Integration Test Results\n\n```\nTest 1 - Valid YAML:      stdout=\"Valid YAML: /tmp/test_valid.yaml\"           exit=0  [PASS]\nTest 2 - Invalid YAML:    stderr=\"Invalid YAML: /tmp/test_invalid.yaml\"       exit=1  [PASS]\n                           stderr=\"  Error: YAML Parse error: Unexpected token\"\nTest 3 - File not found:  stderr=\"Error: File not found: /tmp/nonexistent_file.yaml\"  exit=2  [PASS]\nTest 4 - No arguments:    stderr=\"Usage: bun run validate-yaml <file> ...\"    exit=2  [PASS]\n```\n\n### Dependency Comparison\n\nOriginal `package.json` (main branch):\n```json\n{\n  \"devDependencies\": { \"@types/bun\": \"latest\" }\n}\n```\n\nWorktree `package.json` (feature branch):\n```json\n{\n  \"devDependencies\": { \"@types/bun\": \"latest\" }\n}\n```\n\nResult: Zero new dependencies. Only change is the addition of the `\"validate-yaml\"` script.\n"
